{{!-- Single document shell for every locale. {{{body}}} resolves inside a partial
     called from a layout (verified against Ghost 6.67), so default.hbs and the locale
     shells are one-liners that differ only in the document language.
     `documentLang` is the BCP-47 tag for the collection's language; the default shell passes
     the site locale. It also decides the island strings and the theme toggle's labels, so
     a locale shell is what makes a page fully Spanish/Portuguese rather than half of it.

     Why the fallback is the site locale and not the post's language: a layout cannot
     see the post context. {{#has}} in a layout is always false, {{#post}} yields nothing
     there, and a {{#contentFor}} does reach the layout but is evaluated in the layout's
     own context, so a tag test inside it is false too (all three verified against Ghost
     6.67). The remedy is the documented one: a locale template on the post — which is
     what custom-es.hbs is — or on the page, which is what custom-page-es.hbs is.
     See docs/v3-roadmap.md, Phase 4 notes. --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{#if documentLang}}{{documentLang}}{{else}}{{@site.locale}}{{/if}}">

<head>
    {{!-- `locale` is threaded through unchanged: head.hbs and the islands it configures
         need the page's language, and this is the only level that knows it. It is the
         content-locale key (es/br/en), not the BCP-47 tag — see default-br.hbs. --}}
    {{> "head" locale=locale}}
</head>

{{!-- Two traps in one line, both measured against Ghost 6:
       * the helper only runs as a subexpression here. In a condition position Handlebars
         resolves a bare name against the context, so `{{#if body_class}}` is always false
         and silently drops every context class (post-template, tag-*, paged).
       * it returns a SafeString, which is truthy even on the error context where its value
         is empty — so `{{#if (body_class)}}` is true there too and leaves a stray leading
         space. Comparing the value is what tells the two cases apart. --}}
<body class="{{#match (body_class) "!=" ""}}{{body_class}} {{/match}}bg-surface text-strong antialiased font-sans">

    {{> "header" locale=locale}}

    <main id="main-wrapper" class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-6 relative mt-4">
        {{{body}}}
    </main>
    {{> "footer"}}

    {{ghost_foot}}

    {{> "scripts"}}
</body>

</html>
